---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Roof-Level Forming & Under-Ceiling Applications"
  description="Plan equipment around roof-panel forming or under-ceiling work. Review machine interfaces, panel handover, site access, support and overhead clearance with ARCLIFT."
  transparentNav={false}
>
  <section class="a2-page-head a2-shell">
    <p class="a2-eyebrow">Applications / Start with the work</p>
    <h1>Roof-level forming.<br />Under-ceiling access.</h1>
    <p class="a2-lead">Two different tasks, two different equipment conversations. Define what moves, where it works and which interfaces need review.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="a2-band" data-application-route="roof-forming">
    <div class="a2-shell a2-split">
      <figure class="a2-application-photo">
        <img src="/images/equipment/elevated-roll-forming-platform.jpg" width="349" height="405" alt="Raised equipment platform above a crawler-mounted lifting structure in a yard" fetchpriority="high" />
        <figcaption class="a2-caption">Raised equipment reference in a yard—not evidence of roof-panel production or project suitability.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <div class="a2-split-copy">
        <p class="a2-eyebrow">Primary application / Roof-level roll forming</p>
        <h2>Position the forming machine.<br />Plan the panel's next move.</h2>
        <p>The brief connects the roll former, its mounting arrangement, the required outlet position and the roof receiving area. Crawler and truck-mounted systems are different equipment routes—not interchangeable site approvals.</p>
        <dl class="application-inputs"><div><dt>Machine</dt><dd>Weight, dimensions, mounting and feed direction.</dd></div><div><dt>Workface</dt><dd>Output datum, roof edge and panel handover.</dd></div><div><dt>Site</dt><dd>Access route, setup space, support and transport.</dd></div></dl>
        <div class="a2-actions"><a href="/applications/warehouse/" class="a2-button">Warehouse & industrial roofs</a><a href="/blog/roof-level-roll-forming-long-panels/" class="a2-text-link">Read the planning guide →</a></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="a2-shell a2-section" id="ceiling-access">
    <div class="a2-split">
      <div class="a2-split-copy">
        <p class="a2-eyebrow">Separate application / Under-ceiling access</p>
        <h2>A larger work area.<br />A different set of inputs.</h2>
        <p>Large-deck platforms bring deck layout, overhead clearance and the building-entry route into focus. Main-deck and extension-zone load conditions need separate confirmation.</p>
        <p>A room or building type does not establish equipment suitability. Keep floor information, access constraints and the work-zone plan with the proposed configuration.</p>
      </div>
      <figure class="a2-ceiling-photo"><img src="/images/equipment/under-ceiling-large-deck.jpg" width="611" height="452" alt="Large-deck platform beneath a building's steel roof structure" loading="lazy" /><figcaption class="a2-caption">Under-ceiling equipment reference—not a claimed ARCLIFT project or a capacity statement.</figcaption></figure>
    </div>
    <div class="application-destinations">
      <article data-application-route="stadium-access"><p class="a2-eyebrow">Large-span interiors</p><h3>Stadium & arena</h3><p>Review changing work zones, bearing information, overhead services and recovery arrangements.</p><a href="/applications/stadium/" class="a2-text-link">Review stadium access →</a><a href="/blog/stadium-ceiling-access-platform-planning/" class="a2-text-link">Planning guide →</a></article>
      <article data-application-route="airport-access"><p class="a2-eyebrow">Occupied-building interfaces</p><h3>Airport terminal</h3><p>Review entry clearances, floor information, power requirements and constrained work windows.</p><a href="/applications/airport/" class="a2-text-link">Review airport access →</a><a href="/blog/airport-terminal-maintenance-access-planning/" class="a2-text-link">Planning guide →</a></article>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="a2-inquiry">
    <div class="a2-shell a2-inquiry-inner"><h2>Bring the machine<br />and site into one brief.</h2><div><p>ARCLIFT is an integrated equipment supplier and technical selection and supply partner. Start with non-sensitive project inputs; configuration and site approvals remain separate review steps.</p><a class="a2-button a2-button--orange" href="/contact/">Discuss your application</a></div></div>
  </section>
  <style>
    .a2-application-photo { background: #fff; padding: 28px; }
    .a2-application-photo img { max-width: 320px; width: 100%; height: auto; margin-inline: auto; object-fit: contain; }
    .application-inputs { margin-top: 24px; }
    .application-inputs>div { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 95px minmax(0,1fr); gap: 20px; padding: 12px 0; border-top: 1px solid #c4d0d7; }
    .application-inputs dt { color: #123b50; font-weight: 600; }
    .application-inputs dd { margin: 0; color: #526570; font-size: 17px; }
    .application-destinations { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr)); gap: 48px; margin-top: 52px; }
    .application-destinations article { border-top: 1px solid #c4d0d7; padding-top: 24px; }
    .application-destinations h3 { color: #123b50; font-size: 32px; }
    .application-destinations article>p:not(.a2-eyebrow) { margin: 16px 0; color: #526570; max-width: 52ch; }
    .application-destinations .a2-text-link { margin-right: 24px; }
    @media(max-width:600px) { .application-destinations { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 32px; margin-top: 36px; } .a2-band .a2-split-copy { order: -1; } .application-inputs>div { grid-template-columns: 75px minmax(0,1fr); gap: 16px; } }
  </style>
</BaseLayout>
